repository-code: "https://github.com/carlzimmerman/zimmerman-formula"
abstract: |
  A self-verifying research programme on one claim: the galactic acceleration
  scale is set by the dark-energy density, a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda)
  = c^2 sqrt(Lambda/32 pi) = 9.36e-11 m/s^2 (kappa = 1/2 adopted; measured
  0.551 +/- 0.043 by a distance-free method — fitted, not derived). The
  relativistic realisation embeds the scale in Aether-Scalar-Tensor theory
  (Skordis & Zlosnik 2021) with the promotion a0^2(Q) = kappa^2 G (-K(Q)):
  the MOND scale is the dark sector's pressure, giving a derived a0(z) that
  is flat below z ~ 17-35 and off at recombination. Every load-bearing claim
  is backed by a committed script that exits non-zero on a failed check;
  withdrawn claims are recorded in RETRACTIONS.md. Code is AGPL-3.0; prose,
  papers and figures are CC-BY-4.0.
keywords:
